  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>Jas. Kean, bootmaker, is listed at No. 185 <ref target="civic?id=Queensberry%20Street">Queensberry Street</ref> in 1915.</p>
        <p>James Kean, bootmaker, is also listed at No. 86 <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> in 1910. That may be the same man.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>James O'Maley Kean, bootmaker, is on the 1919 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 185 Queensberry Street, with Jessie Kean, home duties.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>Mrs Ann Hehir is at No. 183 and Mrs Frances Lee at No. 187 in 1915.</p>
      </div>
